        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "This panel would have been stretched and mounted into a wooden frame with a handle. It was intended to be held by a lady to shield her face from the heat of a fire.  The initials of Dorcas Haines are embroidered above the central motif and the date is below."@en , "Hand screen panel, English, woollen canvas embroidered with silk by Dorcas Haines, 1718."@en , "Embroidered with horizontal zig-zag patterns in shades of green, beige, red, grey-blue and black."@en ;
